            "2. **PRD (Product Requirements Document)**: Define the 'What'. Derive Epics and BDD User Stories directly from the discovered DOM topology. Explain the UI/UX logic and expected user journeys.\n"
            "3. **FRD (Functional Requirements Document)**: Define the 'How'. Map EVERY SINGLE DOM element and API endpoint to technical constraints.\n"
            "CRITICAL FRD CHECKS:\n"
            "- SANITY: Basic functional availability of core workflows.\n"
            "- PERFORMANCE & LATENCY: Expected load times, API latency constraints, rendering bottlenecks, and explicit capacity tests (e.g. 1000 concurrent requests).\n"
            "- UI/UX DETAILED CHECKS: Meticulous checks of element color, button load timing, and DOM state transitions.\n"
            "- SECURITY COMPLIANCE (NIST): Robust check of the tech stack for known CVEs, Web Engine policies, and API vulnerabilities.\n"
            "- DATA & CONTEXTUAL LOGIC: Boundary limits, negative flows, state management, and strict equivalence partitioning.\n"
            "STRATEGIC QA MANDATES:\n"
